---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";

/**
 * The front door.
 *
 * Every claim on this page is checkable against a file in this org:
 * `mzizi-dev/mzizi/CHARTER.md` for what Mzizi is and what it has not yet
 * proven, and the repositories themselves for the rest. Nothing here is
 * measured, because nothing has been measured yet — see the status panel,
 * which is the single most important block on the site.
 */

// Where each surface is served from, and whether that hostname resolves today.
// Checked with `dig`, not assumed: as of the last edit, only mzizi.dev and
// mcp.mzizi.dev have DNS records. Anything marked planned is a repository that
// exists and builds, not a name someone reserved.
const surfaces = [
  {
    what: "This site",
    host: "mzizi.dev",
    repo: "mzizi-site",
    live: false,
    note: "The apex currently serves the registry. See the repo README for what a cutover involves.",
  },
  {
    what: "Registry and design system",
    host: "mzizi.dev",
    repo: "mzizi-registry",
    live: true,
    note: "Components, brand, tokens, the DNA-helix architecture, and the /api/v1 the apex serves today.",
  },
  {
    what: "Registry API",
    host: "api.mzizi.dev",
    repo: "mzizi-api-gateway",
    live: false,
    note: "A pure-Rust Cloudflare Worker. Built; the hostname does not resolve yet.",
  },
  {
    what: "Console",
    host: "app.mzizi.dev",
    repo: "mzizi-console",
    live: false,
    note: "Astro chrome, Rust/Dioxus islands. Built; the hostname does not resolve yet.",
  },
  {
    what: "Documentation",
    host: "docs.mzizi.dev",
    repo: "mzizi-docs",
    live: false,
    note: "Repository exists and holds a licence and a README. There is no docs site yet.",
  },
  {
    what: "MCP server",
    host: "mcp.mzizi.dev",
    repo: null,
    live: true,
    note: "Live and OAuth-gated: an unauthenticated request answers invalid_token.",
  },
];
---

<Site
  title="Mzizi"
  description="Mzizi is a Rust framework for the agentic web — a language, compiler and IR designed for machine authorship. A Bundu Foundation research project."
  lede="A Rust framework for the agentic web, designed for machine authorship — and the ecosystem built around it."
>
  <p>
    Every web framework in use today was designed on the assumption that a human
    is typing: reading docs, holding context in their head, tolerating a few
    seconds per compile. Mzizi starts from a different bottleneck — an agent
    iterating against a compiler thousands of times, where compile speed, the
    information density of an error message, and how many tokens a codebase
    costs to read are first-order metrics rather than nice-to-haves.
  </p>

  <p>
    That is the whole of the claim, and it is a narrow one on purpose. Mzizi is
    a language, a compiler and an intermediate representation. It is not a
    rendering engine (it lowers to Dioxus), not an ML runtime (Candle is the
    dependency), and not a post-quantum cryptography project. Those are stated
    non-goals, not omissions.
  </p>

  <div class="status">
    <h2>Status: unmeasured</h2>
    <p>
      The compiler front end exists and is tested — a lexer, a recovering
      parser, an agent diagnostic protocol, a content-addressed IR, and nine
      primitives written in Mzizi itself. Contract blocks parse but are not yet
      evaluated.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong
        >The Phase 0 benchmark has not run, so nothing here has been measured
        against the charter's kill criteria.</strong
      > The charter is explicit that if the benchmark shows no measurable advantage
      over raw Dioxus or Leptos, nothing downstream matters. Treat every claim on
      this site as a design intent with an argument behind it, not a result.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where things are</h2>

  <p>
    Most of this ecosystem is built and not yet routed. The table is honest
    about which is which: <em>live</em> means the hostname resolves and answers,
    <em>planned</em> means the repository exists and builds but DNS does not point
    anywhere yet.
  </p>

  <div class="scroller">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Surface</th>
          <th scope="col">Host</th>
          <th scope="col">State</th>
          <th scope="col">Source</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          surfaces.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">
                {s.what}
                <br />
                <span class="state">{s.note}</span>
              </th>
              <td>
                <code>{s.host}</code>
              </td>
              <td class="state">{s.live ? "● live" : "○ planned"}</td>
              <td>
                {s.repo ? (
                  <a href={`https://github.com/mzizi-dev/${s.repo}`}>{s.repo}</a>
                ) : (
                  <span class="state">not public</span>
                )}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    <a href="/ecosystem">What each repository actually contains →</a>
  </p>

  <h2>For agents</h2>

  <div class="panel">
    <p>
      <a href="/llms.txt"><code>/llms.txt</code></a> is the machine-readable
      summary of this site and the ecosystem it points at — the same facts as
      these pages, without the chrome.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/.well-known/mcp.json"><code>/.well-known/mcp.json</code></a> names
      the one public MCP server in this ecosystem. It requires OAuth; signup is
      free. Discover its tools with the standard <code>tools/list</code> request
      rather than trusting any list written down here, which can go stale.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not hardcode component counts, versions or token values read from any
      page. The registry API is generated from a database and is the only
      authoritative source for them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Two things called Mzizi</h2>

  <p>
    Worth untangling, because the names collide and sources on the web conflate
    them. <strong>Mzizi the framework</strong> — the language, compiler and IR described
    above — is 100% Bundu Foundation IP and is what this page is mostly about. <strong
      >Mzizi the design system</strong
    > is the component registry, brand system and DNA-helix architecture, operated
    by nyuchi, and is what <code>mzizi.dev</code> serves today. They share a name
    and an org; they are different work with different owners.
  </p>
</Site>
